config BOARD_UNAWATCH
    bool
    default y
    select GPIO
    help
      The UNA Watch. The board drives the enables of its loads to their
      off level at boot, as some must not float, which takes the GPIO
      class.

if BOARD_UNAWATCH

config BOARD_UNAWATCH_CONSOLE_DAM
    bool "Console on the USB-C connector"
    default y if !RELEASE
    help
      Drive USB_DAM (PB15) high at boot, which routes the USART3 console
      to the USB-C connector, for a Type-C debug accessory adapter. The
      stock firmware only does so once the STUSB4500 reports a debug
      accessory; without one attached, the console line stays wired to
      the connector.

config BOARD_UNAWATCH_TETHER_SLOT
    bool "Link for the slot of the tether stub"
    help
      Link the image at 0x08080000 instead of 0x08060000, for the slot
      the tether stub (tools/una/tether) programs over USB and starts:
      the stub stays where the bootloader starts images. Such an image
      is flashed with `tether.py flash`, not packed as an .ota.

config BOARD_UNAWATCH_LAB
    bool
    default y if "$(BOARD_VARIANT)" = "lab"
    help
      The experiments firmware, the board's lab variant (unawatch/lab):
      it starts as the first port did, which boots, with the storage in
      the embedded flash, the system resources in the image, the eMMC
      unused at boot and no battery drivers, and carries the Lab app to
      run experiments on the eMMC, the clocks and the reset causes.

endif # BOARD_UNAWATCH
